  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #4490 (UI plan E, #4484) added the in-app menu bar from one command table. sn3ro's UI/UX pre-check of head `3d75878` (comment on #4490, 2026-11-28 01:51Z, with screenshots) found four points in the menu text and structure. They change no command and no ribbon test, so #4490 merges as it is and this issue does the polish.\n\n## Requested\n\n1. **View ▸ Panels and View ▸ Theme:** today a click closes the menu and opens the ribbon's drop-down under its ribbon cell, about 850 px from the click. Make them submenus of View with the same rows as the ribbon lists: the pane check boxes, \"Panel setups…\" and \"Reset layout\" (#4245 names \"View ▸ Reset layout\" for PR P), and the themes and colour-vision rows.\n2. **\"…\" on rows that open a dialog:** the desktop rule is that a row which opens a dialog ends with \"…\", and a row that acts at once does not. Give menu rows their own label in the table (the `Row` type already has a `label` field; `item` reads `text_of`, the ribbon caption today), for example \"Import model…\", \"Open…\", \"Save As…\", \"Post…\". The ribbon keeps its short captions.\n3. **Groups:** add a `group` field (or separator rows) to the table, for example:\n   - File: New, Open… | Save, Save As… | Import model… | Post… | Quit;\n   - Edit: Undo, Redo | Copy, Paste, Delete.\n4. **\"Generate\" in place of \"Run\":** the status words decided on #4245 are \"Up to date\" and \"Needs regenerate\". The menu (and the ribbon) should say \"Generate\" for the command that makes a toolpath, so that the words agree. Check the other places that say \"Run\" for this command (hover texts, status bar, MCP descriptions stay as they are unless they show to the user).\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests: View ▸ Panels and View ▸ Theme open submenus with the ribbon's rows; each dialog row ends with \"…\" and no act-at-once row does; the groups and separators appear in the stated order; the command that generates is named \"Generate\" in the menu and the ribbon.\n- The test that the ribbon and the menu list the same command ids still passes.\n- Layout tests of the menu bar updated. The `crates/ui` test count does not go down (#1953).\n- Before and after screenshots.\n\nCredit: the findings come from sn3ro's review. After #4490 merges. If PR F1 (#4493, \"Settings…\" row) has merged by then, include its row in the groups.\n",
